I read the saved run's plan and the source files. Nothing has been written yet.

**What the plan found**
- **Fixable:** 11 findings in 5 files.
  - Duplicate title: `/about` and `/products`.
  - Duplicate meta description: `/about`, `/products`, `/products/alpha` and `/products/beta`.
  - Missing canonical: `/about`, `/products`, `/products/alpha` and `/products/beta`.
  - Missing sitemap, plus the `robots.ts` line that names it.
- **Not fixable:** none.
- **Out of scope, left alone:** `links.internal.broken` (1), `seo.https.site_not_https` (1) and `seo.content.thin` (7).
- **Deployed address:** `https://www.example.com`, which you gave as an argument. `layout.tsx` already sets `metadataBase` to that address, so the layout needs no change.
- **Saved crawl:** it is no longer stored, so I worked from the source files.

All titles and descriptions below are my suggestions. They are not measured, and they don't change a score.

**1. `src/app/about/page.tsx`**: fixes the duplicate title, the duplicate description and the missing canonical for `/about`.
```diff
+import type { Metadata } from 'next';
+
+// Suggested wording; adjust as you like.
+export const metadata: Metadata = {
+  title: 'About',
+  description: 'About Acme Fixture: a fictional widget maker that exists to show what an SEO audit finds.',
+  alternates: { canonical: '/about' },
+};
+
 // Deliberate problem: no metadata of its own, so the page shows the layout's
 // default title and description, which /products shows too, and it has no
 // canonical link.
```

**2. `src/app/products/page.tsx`**: fixes the duplicate title, the duplicate description and the missing canonical for `/products`.
```diff
+import type { Metadata } from 'next';
 import Link from 'next/link';
 import { PRODUCTS } from '@/lib/products';

+// Suggested wording; adjust as you like.
+export const metadata: Metadata = {
+  title: 'Products',
+  description: 'The Acme Fixture widget range: the small Alpha Widget for desks and the large Beta Widget for workshops.',
+  alternates: { canonical: '/products' },
+};
+
 // Deliberate problem: no metadata of its own (same title and description as
 // /about) and no canonical link.
```

**3. `src/app/products/[id]/page.tsx`**: fixes the duplicate description and the missing canonical for `/products/alpha` and `/products/beta`. Both values are built from the product and the route's `id`, so they differ on each page.
```diff
   const product = findProduct(id);
   if (!product) return {};
-  return { title: product.name };
+  return {
+    title: product.name,
+    // Suggested wording: the product's own summary.
+    description: product.summary,
+    alternates: { canonical: `/products/${id}` },
+  };
 }
```

**4. `src/app/sitemap.ts`** (new file): fixes the missing sitemap. Product addresses come from `PRODUCTS`. `/blog/hello-widgets` is hardcoded because `POSTS` in the blog page isn't exported. If you add posts later, this list needs updating.
```diff
+++ src/app/sitemap.ts
+import type { MetadataRoute } from 'next';
+import { PRODUCTS } from '@/lib/products';
+
+const SITE = 'https://www.example.com';
+
+export default function sitemap(): MetadataRoute.Sitemap {
+  const paths = ['/', '/about', '/blog', '/blog/hello-widgets', '/products'];
+  return [
+    ...paths.map((path) => ({ url: `${SITE}${path}` })),
+    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({ url: `${SITE}/products/${product.id}` })),
+  ];
+}
```

**5. `src/app/robots.ts`**: names the sitemap in `robots.ts`.
```diff
-// Deliberate problem: no sitemap line, and the project has no sitemap.
 export default function robots(): MetadataRoute.Robots {
-  return { rules: [{ userAgent: '*', allow: '/' }] };
+  return {
+    rules: [{ userAgent: '*', allow: '/' }],
+    sitemap: 'https://www.example.com/sitemap.xml',
+  };
 }
```
I also dropped the "Deliberate problem" comment because it stops being true. Say if you'd rather I keep it.

Nothing will be committed or staged.

**Which should I apply: all, some (name the file numbers), or none?** If you apply any, I'll then ask before starting the local server for the re-audit.
